            "review_text": "EVA122014\nItaly24364 contributions\n27\nVietnamese restaurant at the foot of Bitexco Tower, Ho Chi Minh City\nDec 2024 • Couples\nWe spotted this lovely Vietnamese Restaurant already a few days before walking in Ho Chi Minh reading the varied menu on display, we went one evening, and had dinner on the very nice and tastefully decorated outdoor veranda. We ordered , Vietnamese Tacos with Fantastic squid and that I recommend , also beautiful on the eye, rice noodles sautéed with vegetables , very good , however I ordered a carry with coconut milk and seafood , presented in a fresh coconut , the problem that the dish was not as I thought , (it is a dish that I often order abroad and is never a soup with coconut water but a cream with curry and coconut milk so thick ) also inside the coconut the seafood was really non-existent 3 tentacles of octopus and a shrimp with two croutons , I left it whole because it was not to my taste , I really appreciated the gesture of the waiter who was sorry because I had not eaten it and to apologize for the inconvenience offered me a dessert , which was delicious. So just for this I would come back another 100 times and recommend it for the attention to the customer they had. The restaurant is located at the foot of the Bitexco Tower , the inside overlooks a shopping mall the outside on the street , not to be confused with other RuNam around the city.\nRead more\nTranslated from Italian\nShow original\nWritten January 17, 2025",
